Module ombra "The Book of Faces" {
  // ── The hour before ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // From ten to midnight on the ninth night, what became of the city's people is told, as the city tells it, wherever the
  // company is. These are the Registry's, the Watch's and the Serene's; every other thread tells its own people's in its own
  // file with the same newsHour().
  Rule news_marrick_unsaid when newsHour() and knows(party, marrick_was_treasurer) and not wayOpenBook(party) once says "Of Ysolde Marrick: she is buried on the Chapel's north side, in the plot that is kept for Registrars, and the stone says only REGISTRAR. A woman in grey comes at the Ninth Bell on the first night and puts a trimmed lamp on it. The Chaplain, who sees her, says nothing; it is not allowed to say who she is." { }
  Rule news_marrick_named when newsHour() and wayOpenBook(party) once says "Of Ysolde Marrick: her name is on the stone, now, in letters a hand high, and under it, a little smaller, TREASURER, and under that, a little smaller, REGISTRAR. People have begun to leave lamp-wicks on it, the old trimmers' offering, tied in knots. Nobody can say who started it." { }
  Rule news_marrick_unknown when newsHour() and not knows(party, marrick_was_treasurer) and not wayOpenBook(party) once says "Of the Registrar: she is buried on the Chapel's north side under a stone that says REGISTRAR, and the city does not know that it is mourning a lamp-trimmer's daughter, and does it with a great deal of grace." { }
  Rule news_hobb_came when newsHour() and hobbComes(party) once says "Of Hobb the cooper: he called the Urn on the ninth night in a voice that shook only on the last syllable, and was a cooper again by Thursday. He has been seen to take his hat off in the street, which in Ombra is a thing a man does only when he is quite sure." { }
  Rule news_hobb_gave when newsHour() and hobbGaveMask(party) once says "Of Hobb the cooper: he has made a barrel for every house in Counting Row that asked, and charged for none. When asked whom he served, he said: nobody. He is a great deal heavier, and sings." { }
  Rule news_hobb_absent when newsHour() and not hobbComes(party) and not hobbGaveMask(party) and met(hobb) once says "Of Hobb the cooper: he sat in the Serene's mask in his cooperage through the ninth night with the doors barred, hearing a Drawing he did not attend, and at midnight, when the Offices dissolved, he took it off and wept into it, and has been a long time getting his hands to stop." { }
  Rule news_vane_held when newsHour() and vaneHolds(party) and not wayOpenBook(party) once says "Of Orsolya Hart: the Candid hold the Book in the Reading-room under two locks, and she has not opened it again. She says it is a way of keeping a promise. She is seen to look at the shelf the way one looks at a loaded thing." { }
  Rule news_vane_read when newsHour() and vaneHolds(party) and wayOpenBook(party) once says "Of Orsolya Hart: she has taken to wearing a mask in the evenings. She says it is a rest. The Candid have not understood this, and she has not explained." { }
  Rule news_vane_refused when newsHour() and vaneDoubts(party) and not vaneHolds(party) once says "Of Orsolya Hart: she has put out a new pamphlet, in which for the first time the word *consent* appears eleven times. It is her worst-selling." { }
  Rule news_vail_trust when newsHour() and vailTrust(party) >= 3 once says "Of Sergeant Ottoline Vail: the Captain has asked her whom she was talking to in the Gatehouse in the small hours, and she has said, truthfully, the kettle." { }
  Rule news_vail_cold when newsHour() and vailTrust(party) < 3 and warrantHeld(party) once says "Of the Watch: it has filed the Warrant, as it files everything, under W, and the sergeant has gone back to the Customs Steps, where she stands with her hands behind her, looking along the line of the wet and unwanted for the next one." { }
  Rule news_lacke_named when newsHour() and lackeNamedAtHearing(party) once says "Of Corvin Lacke: the name was cried in the Drip by dusk, and by the next evening there was a queue outside his house with a list. He is understood to have left by water. Nobody has been able to find his clocks." { }
  Rule news_lacke_spent when newsHour() and lackeSpentAtHearing(party) once says "Of Corvin Lacke: the Key is Spent, and there is a cooper's-mark on a new clock-mender's shop in Counting Row, and a man behind its window with a loupe in his eye who is exceedingly good at it. He does not look up when the Watch goes by. They do not look in." { }
  Rule news_urn_empty when newsHour() and knows(party, urn_hollow) and not wayHonest(party) once says "Of the Urn: it stands on its plinth in the Urn Hall under a fresh bare oval of wax, as it always has, as heavy as the bronze it is. The Chaplain has suggested, mildly, that it be moved to a museum. The Chapel has declined." { }
  Rule news_urn_filled when newsHour() and wayHonest(party) once says "Of the Urn: they have put forty thousand tesserae in it, and a boy of nine with a very dirty face has been given the key to the lectern in which the Chaplain keeps the list. The Urn rattles, now. People come and shake it, as they would shake a child's money-box, to hear it." { }
  Rule news_the_city_calm when newsHour() and drawingHeld(party) and calm() once says "Of the night: nobody died. By the Chaplain's count that is the first Drawing in forty years of which that can be said, and he has had it written in the Chapel's book in the white ink that is kept for such things." { }
  Rule news_the_city_uneasy when newsHour() and drawingHeld(party) and uneasy() once says "Of the night: two people were hurt on the Chapel steps and one on the Hill stair, and a great deal of the Drip's glass was broken. By the Watch's count it is a good Drawing." { }
  Rule news_the_city_riot when newsHour() and drawingHeld(party) and riotous() once says "Of the night: the Chapel's doors were off their hinges by eleven. There are eight dead, and some forty in the Hospice and the Watch-house, and a great many people who said later that they had been somewhere else, in masks. The Drawing was held. It was, in the Watch's phrase, completed." { }
  Rule news_the_city_none when newsHour() and not drawingHeld(party) once says "Of the night: nobody drew, and the Urn Hall sat until the Ninth Bell struck midnight with a very great many people in it, saying nothing." { }
}
